{"step_index":295,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T19:46:16Z","thinking":"**Investigating search query behavior**\n\nThe observed behavior suggests an issue when filtering by area and search terms simultaneously. Specifically, searching for \"medcare\" or \"lazz pharma\" returns no results in the \"Mirpur, Dhaka\" area, despite the known presence of pharmacies. This indicates the query logic in the backend might be incorrectly applying filters or misinterpreting the search parameters.\n\n\n**Analyzing filter interaction issues**\n\nIt's likely the area filter is overly restrictive when combined with medicine and pharmacy name searches. The screenshots confirm that the lack of results stems from pharmacies not matching the selected area. This suggests the query logic requires all filters to be simultaneously true, leading to zero results when a pharmacy isn't in the specified area, even if it carries the medicine.\n\n\n**Improving search interaction and data**\n\nThe current search implementation requires the user to either press Enter or click a button, which is not intuitive for a good user experience. Implementing a debounced live search, along with medicine autocomplete suggestions, will improve the usability. Additionally, populating Mirpur branches with data for major pharmacy chains and implementing a backend fallback to search other areas if an exact match in the selected area is not found should improve search result completeness.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"filterMedicine\"","SearchPath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\client\"","toolAction":"\"Search filterMedicine in client\"","toolSummary":"\"Search filterMedicine in client\""}}]}
